"""B02B-PASK(LF)(SN) - JST PA series 2-pin 2.00 mm top-entry through-hole header. Bare part.

Datasheet: JST PA connector catalogue (URL in pcb.toml). Ratings from the LCSC C158050
listing: 2 positions, 2.00 mm pitch, 3 A, 250 V, -25 to +85 C, tin-plated, through hole.
TODO: confirm current rating and wire range against the JST PA catalogue.

Footprint: 0.7 mm holes, 1.2 mm pads, 2.00 mm pitch; pad 1 round, pad 2 square. Pin
numbers are the footprint pad numbers.

The same part serves as battery and motor connector, so the reference prefix is a config:
"J" for the battery connector, "M" for the motor and fan connectors.
"""

prefix = config(str, default="J", allowed=["J", "M"], help="Reference designator prefix")

P1 = io(Net)
P2 = io(Net)

Component(
    name="B02B-PASK",
    prefix=prefix,
    symbol=Symbol(library="B02B-PASK.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("JST_PA_B02B-PASK_1x02_P2.00mm_Vertical.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="B02B-PASK(LF)(SN)", manufacturer="JST"),
    pins={"Pin_1": P1, "Pin_2": P2},
    type="connector",
)
